# apps/mobile/android and apps/mobile/ios are LOCAL, UNTRACKED prebuild
# output (never `git add`-ed — a fresh checkout never has them). When
# present, EAS Build treats the project as "bare workflow" and reuses this
# native project AS-IS instead of running its own managed `expo prebuild`
# from app.config.ts. A stale local prebuild (e.g. predating a dependency
# added since) then fails with real but misleading Gradle/CocoaPods errors
# ("No matching variant of project :react-native-async-storage_async-
# storage was found" — confirmed via EAS build b869706a-47a2-4027-9218-
# c25988c085de: the stale android/settings.gradle has zero reference to
# async-storage, autolinking never registered it). Excluding both forces
# EAS to always generate a fresh native project for every build.
apps/mobile/android/
apps/mobile/ios/
